I learned and I think he learned as well  you know one of the funny jokes somebody  told me was they said in Washington if  you want to keep a secret between three  people two of them have to be dead right  and so you know but it wasn't quite that  bad I think it was a function of in the  beginning I felt very very helpless  right like I said I think something and  like it would link to the Washington  Post it was so bad yeah and I think with  him too so so a couple of things I again  I read about how I adjusted and said  okay the game is the game it's been here  long before me it's gonna be here long  after me you know you have a chance to  be in the game if you are in the game  you can get good things done but you  have to get better at the game  so then the campaign's starting and I've  talked to Don Jr about this publicly on  this show and privately like he was  telling me how so many people that were  lifelong friends has suddenly deserted  him and just all of that nonsense so now  you and Ivanka are intimately involved  in this thing and then he wins now  you're going to DC I mean first off did  you have just a whole bunch of friends  that shed you immediately and how insane  was just getting to DC and then seeing  what that was like so believe it or not  we didn't and I think that what what  happened was is I think through my  father's experience I was very selective  in who I let in so Ivanka and I have a  very uh close relationship and a lot of  our time in New York we spent just the  two of us right if we had to choose to  go into a dinner party or being with us  we would be with us and we would always  love doing different Adventures going on  dates you know trying new restaurants  seeing new neighborhoods and then as we  started building a family that was a  priority for us as well and we'd had a  ton of acquaintances you know from New  York but uh but the people who are our  real friends were people who we thought  were very quality people who we got  things out of and and I think who got  things out of us and those people were  all people mostly on the left of the  political Spectrum again I had probably  one conservative friend that I could  think of from before this experience but  everyone was very respectful and very  very open of what we were doing and  recognized that again it wasn't Ivanka  and I who were you know giving speeches  or making policies it was her father and  you know she was doing what uh what a  devoted daughter would do  um but for me I was much more  open-minded and much much more  uh studying the policies I think for  Ivanka she basically said okay if this  is the situation that's happening she  had a mission-driven business at the  time where there were issues she was  advocating for she said well if I can  use this as a platform to elevate the  issues like she cared about like paid  family leave and  um and and child care  um she says well then I think it's kind  of irresponsible not to do that so she  gave a speech at the RNC introducing her  father and all the things on the  internet after was saying was did she  think she was at the Democratic  Convention because they were not  traditionally right Republican policies  um and that her dad used to be loved by  the Democrats I mean there's no shortage  of pictures of with all those people  when they used to love him and he was  donating to some of them yeah being in  New York and again he was part of Pop  Culture yeah so yeah but but the short  answer is is that you know our friends  were were really strong and and really  still are and uh what I found is that  um when we decided to go to Washington  and I write about kind of how we made  that decision because it wasn't like we  were thinking okay he's going to win and  then this is going to happen right the  whole campaign was like let's get to  goal line plus an inch like you know who  the hell knows how this is going to work  out but you do talk about that you kind  of thought it was going to happen the  whole time right I didn't again  logically it felt like he should be able  to do it right all the math and I I can  go to a whole thing on polling but  from what I saw was like the polling all  seemed like it was not scientific right  so if you look at all the public polling  that predicted he was going to lose I  was shocked by how many people just  followed it but polling is basically you  call 500 people and they say yes or no  and then you have to do something called  uh awaiting right and waiting is  basically you say okay this is what okay  if we called you know 100 Democrats and  100 Republicans how many people who  think are going to vote and then you  kind of recalculate the the results in  order to do that so what happened in  brexit right before Trump won was  the polling was off massively now it  predicted the amount of people who said  stay pretty accurately but it was off by  about 3 million votes for the people who  predicted to leave and as we I  researched why that was I was reading  all the the info on it it basically said  that they just under counted low  propensity voters and so with Trump uh  all the media was using basically the  Obama Romney turnout model and I was  like I don't think that's indicative  right like Obama had a different  electricity that Hillary didn't have and  and Trump had a different electricity  that Romney didn't have so it felt like  it should be different and then when I  look at we had a data we built a data  file about 10 million people were  showing up to Trump rallies and a big  percentage of them were low propensity  voters and so we basically every time we  do a sample which we we re-engineered  the polling we basically ran it through  two different models one was like the  media model which showed we were going  to lose and what was our model showed we  were going to win and so I just again  you know Romney went into election night  thinking they were going to win if I was  told and then were disappointed so I  never allowed myself to believe our data  because I'd never done it before and so  but that was what I believed was more  logical as an outcome but we didn't  think about what would come next  sorry it's such a long no no So speaking  of what came next so now you get there  and I now you're working for the  president and media is not that happy  CNN New York Times okay all that stuff  but you guys actually were accomplishing  an awful lot pretty much from the gecko  considering you had no nobody willing to  to work with you yeah so it was a wild  thing and and the first year in writing  the book I went through the first year  and it brought back a lot of memories  that actually were really painful for me  because hey we get to Washington so we  make the decision to to and it wasn't  like oh should we stay in New York and  live our lives or should we go to  Washington was like okay he is now going  to be the president United States our  former lives as we knew it don't exist  anymore right so and then you say you  have an opportunity to serve in in  government and try to make an impact and  I build more confidence based on the  fact that on campaign I was able to  achieve certain successes and things  um that experienced political people  told me was the wrong way to do it but  then I did it that way and it ended up  working  and so I said let's give it a shot and  let's try to help him and again you know  he'd never been a mayor never been a  governor so he was running a family  business he was used to working with  family his campaign was a family  campaign and so we said let's go give it  a shot and and really try to see if we  could help him implement the policies  that we believe in and try to do things  that we believe are good so Ivanka gave  up her business to then focus on her  Mission I went in  and we had no idea what a brutal world  uh Washington was going to be and so  whether it was like the attacks from the  media whether it was the investigation I  mean within three months I have you know  people leaking on me like crazy from  inside the White House you know you talk  to yourself and it would be in the  Washington Post uh wait can you just  talk about a little bit more about what  that's like the leak situation like how  is it possible because everyone's always  talking about the leaks they were  talking about an awful lot with Trump  but it happens in every Administration  like  did you feel like oh here's 10 people in  this room in this meeting like six of  them might be the one or like how do you  manage some of that stuff as an advisor  or do you pull him aside and say hey Mr  President maybe don't or dad-in-law or  whatever you call him Don do you maybe  don't say everything you think off the  cuff in front of everybody because we  have this problem like so so I think I  learned and I think he learned as well  you know one of the funny jokes somebody  told me was they said in Washington if  you want to keep a secret between three  people two of them have to be dead right  and so you know but it wasn't quite that  bad I think it was a function of in the  beginning I felt very very helpless  right like I said I think something and  like it would link to the Washington  Post it was so bad yeah and I think with  him too so so a couple of things I again  I write about how I adjusted and said  okay the game is the game it's been here  long before me it's gonna be here long  after me you know you have a chance to  be in the game if you are in the game  you can get good things done but you  have to get better at the game and so  certain things like when I would give my  opinion to Donald especially when I  would disagree with him I would always  do it when I I would never say my  opinion in front of other people or I  would say something that I didn't think  would be salacious but when I wanted to  strongly disagree I would always do it  privately because you never wanted to  read about that in the Press because  that would if you I never wanted  division to to show between us because  he always gave me the opportunity to  voice my opinion and sometimes he would  listen sometimes he wouldn't again I was  an advisor and some things quite frankly  I had more conviction on some things I  had less conviction on and often when he  would ask me I'd say look I'm not an  expert on it let me find somebody who I  think is and bring them in to give you  that point of view um but but so that  was probably number one and then when it  came to just dealing with people you  learned very quickly like who was  leaking to which places and right we  just had so many of them who were  scumbags who were doing that were they  all your guys  you know what I mean or were they were  they like sort of deep State people that  were all there all the time or were they  were there a lot of them were the people  coming in look we we I mean we didn't  have a lot of people right and and you  know the campaign was ragtag uh we had  to staff up quickly or making a lot of  decisions putting different people  together and uh yeah you just have  people and then you know the more people  get insecure the more they it's an  environment that that kind of encourages  more of it so it's it's a very very  complicated situation to work in but  like I said I figured out how to adjust  I got tighter  um and then ultimately over time like  towards the end we we announced a peace  deal which which we'll talk about later  but like and nobody knows about it right  so so I learned how to find the people  who you could work with to keep things  quiet but it just took me some time and  like when you work in you know real  estate or technology like nobody's out  there leaking to the Press right and  everyone's aligned for the same Mission  too so it's just a different game and  you just have to learn to adjust to the  game if you're looking for more honest  and thoughtful conversations about  politics instea